l":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-03-05T01:41:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T20:20:55Z","closed_at":"2026-03-09T20:20:55Z","assignee":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7.dev2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev2 - macOS Tahoe (26.3.0) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (10 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIt appears that Godot is assuming the return types of functions that do not have a return type specified.  This is causing a lot of `Cannot return value of type \"X\" because the function return type is \"Y\"` errors in my plugin (GUT).\n\nI turned all \"Error\" to \"Ignore\" and the issue still happens.\n\nOne simple example is I have a method that the user is expected to override if they want to make GUT skip a test script while running tests.  \n```gdscript\nclass_name GutTest # res://addons/gut/test.gd\n...\nfunc should_skip_script():\n\treturn false\n```\nGUT will skip the script if the user returns `true` or a `String`.  All other values returned are treated as `false`.  The `String` is displayed in the logs if it is returned.  Here are two example implementations given in the wiki:\n```gdscript\nextends GutTest\nfunc should_skip_script():\n    if DisplayServer.get_name() == \"headless\":\n        return \"Skip Input tests when running headless\"\n```\n```gdscript\nextends GutTest\nfunc should_skip_script():\n    return EngineDebugger.is_active()\n```\nIn the editor it marks the string return as an error because it thinks that the return value is a `bool`.\n\n<img width=\"609\" height=\"222\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b86c5c1c-d9a0-4bfc-a409-71f145e3c7f2\" />\n\nThere are zero declarations of `should_skip_script` in the GUT project that have a declared return type.\n\nI attempted to declare a return type of `Variant`, but that causes parsing errors on the `DisplayServer` example, since not all paths return a value.  This would be a feasible workaround, but it isn't a great solution.  There could be many users that are using this example in CICD pipelines.\n\nThis also appears to be affecting my dynamic Script doubling logic as there are many tests failing due to `Cannot return value of type ...` errors, or `A void function cannot return a value.` errors.  I have not looked in that yet though, since the above case is way less complicated.  I imagine it has to do with the fact that return types weren't supplied in the metadata, so all my wrappers `return super()` by default.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n# Successful reproduction\n* clone https://github.com/bitwes/Gut\n* Open the editor\n* Click the \"GUT\" bottom panel\n* Click \"Run All\"\n\n# Failed to reproduce\nI was unable to reproduce the issue with a simple project that had two inner classes in the same file that replicated the definitions of `should_skip_script`.\n\nI was also unable to replicate it with two files with `class_name` that replicated the definitions of `should_skip_script`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nclone https://github.com/bitwes/Gut","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117081/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117081/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}